{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110166","id":2789978773,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6mS7KV","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110166","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110166.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110166.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110166","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110166/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/110166/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110166/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/055470ea6d897c42d83f842e7a4f60d7194e1b33","number":110166,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Handle EOF correctly in StreamPeerBuffer::get_partial_data","user":{"login":"ghost","id":10137,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTM3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10137?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost","html_url":"https://github.com/ghost","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ghost/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This pull request improves EOF handling in StreamPeerBuffer::get_partial_data, ensuring correct error signaling and more robust data reading.\r\n\r\n## Description\r\nThe function now returns ERR_FILE_EOF when the read pointer exceeds the data size, instead of ambiguous or misleading return values. \r\n\r\nThis change clarifies the function's behavior at EOF, prevents potential issues with zero-length reads, and improves error handling consistency. Unnecessary comments have been removed for cleaner code.\r\n\r\n## Motivation\r\nThe previous implementation could return OK even when no data was read, making it difficult for callers to distinguish between a successful read and reaching the end of the buffer. \r\n\r\nBy explicitly returning ERR_FILE_EOF, the code is more predictable and easier to maintain, reducing the risk of subtle bugs and improving overall reliability.","labels":[{"id":73330064,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2NA==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/bug","name":"bug","description":"","color":"ff6055","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":649800701,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDk4MDA3MDE=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:network","name":"topic:network","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-09-01T14:10:45Z","updated_at":"2026-01-13T11:12:13Z","closed_at":"2026-01-13T11:08:09Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"0bcc125efd28c7320379eebd90d8393afb323d39","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_te